(R,"Visit four cities once each and return, with the least cost. Can I avoid trying every order?"),
(S,"Yes, with bitmask dynamic programming. A bitmask is the set of visited cities, and the table remembers the cheapest route for each set and last city. The best tour costs eighty."),
